  (id,opportunity_id,cycle_key,cycle_label,application_year,programme_year,intake_year,application_model,closes_on,closes_at,closes_timezone,programme_starts_on,programme_ends_on,programme_dates_text,application_dates_text,date_precision,duration_text,source_status,audience_text,eligibility_text,right_to_work_text,funding_text,application_process_text,programme_structure_text,official_url,application_url,active,research_checked_on,created_at,updated_at)
values
  ('f82520cb-ec7b-4e66-acd3-bf60a2470b5a','51a9940e-1fa2-40dd-b888-75dd9b253fd7','keating-combar-mentoring:2026-27','COMBAR Mentoring Scheme 2026–27 — Keating Chambers Partner',2026,2026,2026,'fixed_deadline',date '2026-10-23',time '23:59','Europe/London',null,null,'The 2026–27 scheme provides a series of one-to-one mentoring sessions.','Applications close at midnight on 23 October 2026.','exact','2026–27 mentoring cycle','open','Aspiring barristers from groups underrepresented at the Bar, particularly the Commercial Bar.','Applicants must meet the current COMBAR scheme criteria for an underrepresented group. Keating participates as one of the member sets supporting the scheme.',null,null,'Use the guidelines and application form linked from COMBAR’s official scheme announcement.','Successful applicants are paired with practitioners from participating COMBAR member sets for one-to-one mentoring.','https://www.combar.com/news/deadline-extended-to-23-october-2026-combar-mentoring-scheme-for-under-represented-groups-2026-27-scheme/','https://www.combar.com/news/deadline-extended-to-23-october-2026-combar-mentoring-scheme-for-under-represented-groups-2026-27-scheme/',true,date '2026-10-15',now(),now()),
  ('f854ce47-0be3-455b-948e-a4b1644e7b59','19036058-f62e-4a33-8d9d-e3afad2059be','keating-10000-black-interns-bar:2027','10,000 Black Interns — The Bar 2027 — Keating Chambers Partner',2026,2027,2027,'fixed_deadline',date '2026-11-01',null,'Europe/London',date '2027-06-01',date '2027-09-30','Six-week internships take place between June and September 2027, with dates agreed through the programme.','Applications for the Summer 2027 programme close on 1 November 2026.','exact','Six weeks','open','Black university students, postgraduate students, confirmed university entrants on a gap year and recent UK-university graduates.','Applicants must be aged 18 or over, be Black African, Black Caribbean, Black British or of mixed Black heritage, meet the programme’s UK study or recent-graduate criteria, and not previously have secured a 10,000 Black Interns placement.','Applicants must already have unrestricted permission to work full-time in the United Kingdom when applying.','Paid internship at the programme’s applicable rate.','Apply through the 10,000 Interns Foundation and select The Bar workstream. Candidates may choose a region but cannot select an individual chambers.','The Bar workstream rotates interns across chambers and other Bar organisations, providing experience of advocacy, case preparation and legal practice. Keating confirms continuing participation in the programme.','https://10000internsfoundation.com/students-graduates/10000-black-interns/','https://10000internsfoundation.com/students-graduates/10000-black-interns/',true,date '2026-10-15',now(),now());

